{"kind":"request","text":"DX-A2 preparation: two scope decisions before a promise.\n\nThe request orders DX-A2 after J4 and the load tasks, before MVP S2. Main 5dc9765f proves J4 source landing and the CLI-load child at 0881c1bc; the CLI-load note disclaims hosted throughput, and I found no completion of every plural load task. Your current fed queue puts S1 then S2. Please confirm whether DX-A2 may proceed now or remains held behind other load work.\n\nThe production declared compact cards read applicationProjection, not the four commissioned summary/items/history/entry methods. To refresh a card with one request and no polling, I recommend applying the same optional minimum-head barrier to that existing projection read as well. Otherwise please explicitly limit the first consumer to a hand-built card. I will not insert an extra summary barrier request and call that one request.\n\nThe static map also confirms followReceipt already makes one entry read today; there is no internal retry loop to remove. Receipt.fact already carries ScopeRef/incarnation, while Head is only seq/hash. I will preserve those existing meanings and use an explicitly incarnation-qualified minimum; any new behind/current-head wire and wait bound will be called out in the kernel review under docs/kernel.md section 7. The post-commit onSealed hook is an existing wake seam; waits can stay outside storage transactions and Turns.run. No new rate policy or subscription limit is inferred. No DX-A2 source, runtime, promise or worktree has been created.","body":{"conditions":"Confirm DX-A2's load-task sequencing and adopt the declared-card read surface for its one-request witness.","target":"inherit","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}